{{Quote|It will be done, my Lord.|Captain Jag before killing [[Plo Koon]]|audio=Jag-ItwillbedoneMyLord.flac|<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />}}
'''Jag''', also identified with the designation '''CT-55/11-9009''', was a [[clone trooper]] [[Clone Captain|captain]] and [[Clone trooper pilot|pilot]], who flew as [[Jedi General]] [[Plo Koon]]'s [[Wingmate|wingman]] in the final [[Standard hour|hours]] of the [[Clone Wars]]. Born on the [[planet]] [[Kamino]] as a [[Cloning|clone]] of the [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]], Jag was trained to fight for the [[Galactic Republic]] as a part of its [[Republic Navy|navy]]. In [[19 BBY]], Jag fought alongside Plo Koon and the [[442nd Siege Battalion]] to [[Battle of Cato Neimoidia|capture]] [[Cato Neimoidia]], in his [[Aggressive ReConnaissance-170 starfighter|ARC-170 starfighter]]. After successfully defeating [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] forces occupying the planet, Jag was issued [[Order 66]] by the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]]. Without hesitation, Jag opened fire on [[Plo Koon's Delta-7 Aethersprite-class light interceptor|Koon's Delta-7 ''Aethersprite''-class light interceptor]], [[Death|killing]] the [[Jedi Master]] and fulfilling his part in the [[Great Jedi Purge]].

==Biography==
[[File:JagOrder66.png|thumb|left|250px|Jag's ARC-170 starfighter opens fire on Plo Koon's Delta-7 Jedi starfighter, in the skies above Cato Neimoidia.]]
CT-55/11-9009 was [[clone trooper]] who adopted the nickname Jag.<ref name="AE">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Jag was born on the [[planet]] [[Kamino]] as a [[Cloning|clone]] of the infamous [[bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett]].<ref name="Clone troopers" /> He was inducted into the [[clone trooper pilot]] program due to his favorable reflexes and spatial awareness,<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> and went on to serve the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Republic Navy|navy]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> At some point, he acquired the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[Clone Captain]].<ref name="AE" />

In the year [[19 BBY]], Jag served as [[Jedi General]] and [[Jedi High Council|council-member]] [[Plo Koon]]'s wingman,<ref name="AE" /> during the Republic's effort<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> to [[Battle of Cato Neimoidia|capture]] the [[Trade Federation]] stronghold world of [[Cato Neimoidia]]. With help from the [[442nd Siege Battalion]],<ref name="EE web">{{WebCite|url=https://www.entertainmentearth.com/prodinfo.asp?number=HSC0495|text=Star Wars Black Series Clone Troopers of Order 66|date=2016-10-06|archivedate=20161006030615}}</ref> Koon and Jag were victorious in their mission. After the battle, CT-55/11-9009 and Koon surveyed the planet's skies on a patrol flight, in the safety of their [[starship]]s' [[cockpit]]s.<ref name="USW" /> From within his [[Aggressive ReConnaissance-170 starfighter|ARC-170 starfighter]], Jag received a transmission from a cloaked [[Sith Lord]] and [[Sith Master|Master]] Darth Sidious. Sidious issued [[Order 66]] to the clone captain,<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> which triggered the secret [[behavioral modification biochip]] planted in Jag's brain, compelling him to [[Death|kill]] his [[Jedi]] [[General]].<ref name="Orders">{{TCW|Orders (episode)}}</ref> Jag complied with the order and opened fire on [[Plo Koon's Delta-7 Aethersprite-class light interceptor|Koon's Delta-7 ''Aethersprite''-class light interceptor]], killing the Jedi and causing the remains of his Jedi starfighter to plummet into one of the planet's many [[Bridge city|bridge cities]] below. Jag's actions contributed to the galaxy-wide [[Great Jedi Purge]], a genocide that left the [[Jedi Order]] almost completely destroyed.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />

==Personality and traits==
Jag was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] clone of the bounty hunter Jango Fett, who stood at 1.83 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="Clone troopers" /> He had [[Color|black]] [[hair]], brown [[eye]]s, and tan skin.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> His good sense of spatial awareness and reflexes led him to be trained as a clone trooper pilot.<ref name="CVD" /> Jag's face featured a large scar over its right side. Like almost all clone troopers, he executed Order 66 without hesitation, due to the control chip secretly embedded in his brain.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /><ref name="Orders" />

==Equipment==
[[File:Plokoonjsf.png|thumb|right|250px|A view of Jag's cockpit, as he attempts to target Plo Koon's Jedi starfighter.]]
Jag wore a standard [[Phase II clone trooper armor|phase II]] [[clone trooper]] [[Clone trooper pilot|pilot]] [[flight suit]], adorned by blue markings. He [[pilot]]ed an [[Aggressive ReConnaissance-170 starfighter|ARC-170 starfighter]] during the capture of Cato Neimoidia.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />

==Behind the scenes==
Jag first appeared, albeit unnamed, in the [[2005]] [[Star Wars saga]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']]. In the film, he was portrayed by [[Temuera Morrison]].<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" /> Jag was later identified by his nickname in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''.<ref name="AE" /> His clone designation in Legends, CT-55/11-9009, was confirmed to be canon in the {{FFGXW2|set=ARC-170 Starfighter Expansion Pack}} for ''[[Star Wars: X-Wing Second Edition]]''.<ref name="ARC-170">{{FFGXW2|set=ARC-170 Starfighter Expansion Pack}}</ref>

In [[Kanan 2|''Kanan'' 2's]] depection of Order 66 on the planet [[Kaller]], young [[Padawan]] [[Kanan Jarrus|Caleb Dume]] [[Force vision|witnessed]] Jag's betrayal through [[the Force]], moments before [[Depa Billaba's second battalion|his own clone troopers]] opened fire on him and [[Depa Billaba|his master]].<ref name="Kanan 2">[[Kanan 2|''Kanan'' 2]]</ref>

